<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  AIOS — macOS hardened-runtime entitlements (minimal, deliberate).

  Only com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit is granted today: Electron's V8 engine
  requires JIT (write-then-execute memory). This is always needed and is the
  single safe baseline entitlement.

  EMPIRICAL-ADD CANDIDATES — add ONLY if a signed + notarized build later fails
  to sign, or the app fails to launch. These are NOT granted pre-emptively (each
  one weakens the hardened runtime). They are likely to be needed because
  node-pty is a bundled NATIVE module (asarUnpack'd .node binary) and the app
  spawns child processes (the `claude` CLI inside real PTYs):

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
      -> if V8/native code hits W^X errors at launch.
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key><true/>
      -> if child processes need DYLD_* env vars.
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key><true/>
      -> node-pty's native .node / any unsigned dylib the app dlopens.
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.inherit</key><true/>
      -> for spawned children to inherit the parent's entitlements
         (belongs in the entitlementsInherit file; mutually exclusive with
         granting per-binary entitlements, so weigh before adding here).

  Rule: add on EVIDENCE (a real sign/launch failure), not preemptively.

  GRANTED ON EVIDENCE — com.apple.security.device.audio-input.
  Unlike the candidates above, this does not relax code-signing or memory protections: it is a
  resource-access entitlement that only lets the app ASK for the microphone. The operator still
  sees the macOS permission prompt and can refuse. It is needed because macOS attributes a PTY
  child's microphone access to this app (the responsible process), so Claude Code's voice mode
  records under OUR signature. Without it the hardened runtime refuses silently: measured on the
  shipped 0.10.0, AVCaptureDevice.requestAccess(.audio) from a pane returned false in 0.01 s, no
  prompt appeared and the app never showed up in Privacy → Microphone.
  Guarded by src/test/macMicrophone.test.ts (config) and scripts/verify-signing.mjs (artifact).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
